  "body": "Stacked on #3421 (merge #3421 first). This PR adds one commit on top of the #3421 head (`f9b38a9d7`).\n\n## What changed\n- `assets/posts/fanuc.cps`: new function `uprightAfterTilt()`. `startPreamble` calls it directly after the `G90 G54 G40 G49 G80` line, before the tool change.\n- `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps`: the same function and call. A turning A gets `M11` before the return and `M10` after it, as `onRapid` does.\n- The function reads `rotAt` (the angles that the control holds, #885). For each rotary that is not at zero, it writes:\n  - `G91 G28 Z0` and `G90` (or `G53 G00 Z` with the `safeRetract` G53 option);\n  - `G00 <letter>0.` for each rotary that is not at zero.\n- Then it sets `xyUnknown`. The first X/Y traverse states its height again.\n- New test file `crates/post/tests/upright_after_tilt.rs`.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/3466-upright-after-tilt.md`.\n\n## Cause\n- The angle words are modal. A tilted section ends with its exit rapid at the lean.\n- `endPreamble` reset only the memory of the script (`lastA/B/C`), not the control.\n- A 3-axis section that follows states no angle. Thus it cut with the axes still tilted.\n\nFanuc on `tilthead.mch`, before and after (same tool):\n\n| Before (base #3421) | After (this PR) |\n|---|---|\n| `G01 X10. Y0. Z0. B20. F500` | `G01 X10. Y0. Z0. B20. F500` |\n| `G00 X10. Y0. Z20.` | `G00 X10. Y0. Z20.` |\n| `M9` / `M5` | `M9` / `M5` |\n| `(OPERATION: Flat2 - G54)` | `(OPERATION: Flat2 - G54)` |\n| `G90 G54 G40 G49 G80` | `G90 G54 G40 G49 G80` |\n| | `G91 G28 Z0` |\n| | `G90` |\n| | `G00 B0.` |\n| `T01 M6` ... `G00 X30. Y30. Z20.` (still at B20) | `T01 M6` ... `G00 X30. Y30. Z20.` |\n\n## The return between two tilted sections is kept on purpose\nA tilted section that follows a tilted section also gets the return. The second section then states its lean again from a known zero. This is two moves more, and it is safe. The scripts stay simple because they need no look-ahead to the next section.\nThe choice is pinned by:\n- `fanuc_returns_to_zero_between_two_tilted_sections`\n- `doosan_returns_to_zero_between_two_tilted_sections`\n\n## Tests\nPins in `camcraft-post` (red before the fix: yes):\n- `fanuc_states_upright_after_a_tilted_section_with_the_same_tool`\n- `fanuc_states_upright_after_a_tilted_section_with_a_tool_change`\n- `doosan_states_upright_after_a_tilted_section_with_the_same_tool`\n- `doosan_states_upright_after_a_tilted_section_with_a_tool_change`\n- `fanuc_returns_to_zero_between_two_tilted_sections`\n- `doosan_returns_to_zero_between_two_tilted_sections`\n- `tormach_states_upright_after_an_indexed_section` (Tormach was safe by the read in the issue; this pins it)\n- `an_upright_program_after_an_upright_section_writes_no_return` (no rotary word in an upright program)\n\nEach pin checks this order in the next section: a retract (`G28` or `G53`), then the zero word with no X/Y, then the first X/Y traverse, then the first cut.\n\nRed text before the fix: `fanuc (tool 1): the upright section commands A0 B0 before its first cut` (the program had no rotary word between the sections).\n\nMutations:\n- `fanuc.cps` from base: the two Fanuc pins are red. The fix restored: green.\n- `doosan-dnm.cps` from base: the two Doosan pins are red. The fix restored: green.\n\n## Goldens moved\n- `examples/catalog/multiaxis/indexed/indexed.nc`: six lines more, in two sections.\n  - Section \"Back pocket\" (after \"Front pocket\" at A90) gets `G91 G28 Z0`, `G90`, `G00 A0.`.\n  - Section \"Tilted pocket\" (after \"Back pocket\" at A-90) gets the same three lines.\n  - These two sections follow a tilted section, so `uprightAfterTilt()` writes the return. No other line of the file changes.\n  - The case has two tilted sections in a row. It shows the kept choice above.\n  - Regenerated with `cargo xtask catalog --case multiaxis/indexed`.\n\n## Gates on the new head (base `origin/main` `ef1572114`)\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 126 steps, 0 failed (5.6 min). The touched suites are green: `app suites: example_catalog`, `post suites: upright_after_tilt`, `post suites: opening_rotary_pose`, `app suites: opening_rotary_pose`, `post suites: fanuc_post`, `post suites: doosan_dnm_post`, `app suites: conformance`, `app suites: posting`.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base origin/main`: 28 steps, 0 failed (41.7 min). `app heavy: example_catalog` is green. The run also covers `app heavy: conformance` and `app heavy: c_axis_live`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate test catalog_multiaxis_indexed --crate camcraft-app`: 3 tests, 0 failed.\n- `cargo xtask gate test upright --crate camcraft-post` and `cargo xtask gate test returns_to_zero_between_two_tilted --crate camcraft-post`: all pins, 0 failed.\n\n## Not exercised\n- Item 3 of the issue (an app refusal for a post script of the user that does not state the return) is not in this PR. It needs a manifest flag in the engine. Filed as #3477.\n- Mach4 is not pinned. Its AC trunnion fixture is local to `mach4_trunnion.rs`. #3477 lists the pin.\n- The Doosan indexed 4th-axis path (no RTCP, `M10`/`M11`) was not posted in a test that turns only A.\n- A program on a real control. The order is from the post text only.\n\n## Overlaps\n- #3421: this PR is stacked on it (`post/mod.rs` `dump`, `stamp.rs`). This PR does not change those files.\n- #3441 touches `assets/posts/fanuc.cps` `startPreamble` too (it adds `aiccOn()` at the end of the function). Same function, different lines. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: The Fanuc and Doosan DNM posts now return the rotaries to zero at the reference height before an operation that follows a tilted operation, so a 3-axis operation no longer cuts with the axes still tilted.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3466\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
